00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.840
So if you're like most people,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.840
you've had a vision of
your potential future self.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.890
The more successful, better groomed,

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.960
richer, happier version of yourself.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.750
But you've probably also
wondered if you can actually

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.080
become this person

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.180
or if this person is just a figment

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.870
of your reckless imagination.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:26.370
Because sometimes the
contrast between who you are

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.330
and who you want to be seems so stark.

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.800
You wonder if this idea of your potential

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.160
is even attainable

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.740
or is it just an instrument of false hope

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.230
like a carrot to a mule.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.340
After all, while some few
people really do achieve

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.740
their dreams and change the world,

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.210
the vast majority of others don't.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.760
They don't even come close.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.220
So what's the difference between
these two types of people

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:52.100
and how can not let our dreams be dreams

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.600
and actually become the
person we think about

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.940
when the word potential is thrown around?

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.860
Author Jeff Olsen suggests
that there is a reliable tactic

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.200
you can use for achieving success,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.720
whatever that may mean to you.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.440
There is a surefire way
to make massive progress

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.280
in any area of your life

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.700
and it's not as hard as you might think.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.720
So here it goes.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.950
Everyone who has ever been successful

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.780
understood this thing
called the slight edge.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.617
They may not have called
it the slight edge

00:01:20.617 --> 00:01:23.570
but the slight edge was without contention

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:26.210
the main factor in them achieving success.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.190
So how does it work?

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.060
Okay, so say you had a
ridiculously rich uncle

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.200
who is feeling really generous one day

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.757
and he said to you "Kevin my
boy, I'll give you two options.

00:01:35.757 --> 00:01:38.857
"Either I give you one
million dollars cash right now

00:01:38.857 --> 00:01:41.147
"and you can walk out
the door a millionaire

00:01:41.147 --> 00:01:44.437
"or I give you a single penny, one cent

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:47.230
"and I will double it
every day for a month."

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:49.190
That accent was all over the place.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:50.550
Which option would you choose?

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.870
Gut instinct tells you option one

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.540
but if we do some simple math,

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.070
option one gives you one million dollars.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:58.140
That's pretty simple math

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.230
but if you had the
patience and perseverance

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.370
to stick it out for 30 days,

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:05.230
option two gives you $5,386,709.12.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.820
Over five times the value
of option one which is weird

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.780
because with option two,

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.960
for the vast majority of those days,

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.600
this money doubling seems
like a waste of time.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.630
After 20 days of doubling,

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:25.100
you would have only had
a little over $5,000.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.640
At that point, if you were Kevin,

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.240
you definitely would have
thought you screwed up big time.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:32.210
But by sticking with it,
dramatic change happens.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:33.560
So here's another example.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:36.130
Sure you can hit the
gym really hard one day,

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.950
like the best, heaviest
workout of your life.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.340
Just straight barbaric.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.550
And afterwards, you do everything right.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.820
You have a giant, protein-rich meal

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.200
and a long, restful night's sleep.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.510
But unfortunately, even after all that,

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:51.210
you won't see any results.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:54.470
Visually, you'll be just as big
as you were before you went.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:57.200
In fact if you were to skip
the gym that day altogether,

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.360
in the grand scheme of things,

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.180
it wouldn't really make a difference.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.590
If you asked a friend how you looked

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.280
before and after your workout,

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.560
assuming there is no
such thing as being swol,

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.170
they'd say you looked the exact same.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.830
That's because you don't
get to have huge muscles

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.000
by going to the gym
harder than everyone else

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.840
that one time you're motivated
enough to go to the gym.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.310
You get to have huge muscles
by just showing up to the gym

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.820
every single day for
a long period of time.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:23.450
So the slight edge can all
be boiled down to this.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.500
Success is not the result
of doing difficult,

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.010
extraordinary things

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.680
but rather the result
of doing unremarkable,

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.900
relatively easy to do
things every single day

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.480
over a long period of time.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:36.780
Maybe you wanna write a book.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.070
If that's the case, then
you shouldn't think about it

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.410
in terms of somehow possessing
the massive inspiration

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.780
to crank out 200 brilliant
pages of literature

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.490
because you already know
that's never gonna happen.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:49.700
If you wanna write a book,

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:52.120
write half a page and
then be done for the day.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.790
Then when you wake up the next morning,

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.960
finish that page and take a break.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.020
Make writing half a page
into a simple daily habit

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.570
and it will eventually turn
into a well oiled machine

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.490
that will easily take you to your goal.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.930
By casually showing up ever single morning

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:08.580
to write a relatively
easy amount of words,

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:12.642
after a year's time, you will
have written 182.5 pages.

00:04:12.642 --> 00:04:13.940
That's a book!

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.170
And you did it with hardly any strain.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.960
And that's because writing
half a page is easy,

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.120
something you're actually likely to do.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.930
But when leveraged by time,

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.830
half a page turns into a book.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.570
45 minutes at the gym
turns into a beach body.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.460
30 minutes of practicing guitar

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.447
turns into "Holy (beep)
Fred, I didn't know

00:04:31.447 --> 00:04:32.860
"you're such a good musician."

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:35.180
So if you wanna achieve
massive progress in your life

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:36.810
in any particular area,

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.290
break it down into a tiny, little action.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:43.220
Something easy, so easy that
you're actually likely to do it

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.680
but make sure to do it every single day

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.100
because as easy it is to do,

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.120
it's just as easy not to do.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.710
And doing it or not doing
it is the difference

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:55.840
between a life of success
and one of mediocrity

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:56.923
later down the road.

